{"parentUuid":"39b12840-30d4-43ec-89bc-c78778fdb401","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkeKhtCsU4TTSEGXpKzF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KUyxH9PkjtTfWGAouSy9BE","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat /Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory/live-host-check-via-instrumented-dev-page.md /Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory/live-test-built-app-on-mac.md | head -70"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2782,"cache_read_input_tokens":277579,"output_tokens":289,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":127},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2782,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":289,"cache_read_input_tokens":277579,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2782,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2782},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01KUyxH9PkjtTfWGAouSy9BE":{"command":"cat /Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory/live-host-check-via-instrumented-dev-page.md /Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory/live-test-built-app-on-mac.md | head -70"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgkeKhXNrRtkDW6qy6RRi","requestRef":"8dc9dc37-5e36-4c41-9a86-0fbdc2521b28","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"d4534a26-aedc-4972-9564-f0c1cae51c2a","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:24:57.327Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35/build/arm64","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/first-run-printer-step","slug":"dapper-knitting-moler"}
{"parentUuid":"d4534a26-aedc-4972-9564-f0c1cae51c2a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"83c73b6a-60cc-4bfb-ac6c-646bdd504022","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KUyxH9PkjtTfWGAouSy9BE","type":"tool_result","content":"---\nname: live-host-check-via-instrumented-dev-page\ndescription: Test host behaviour in the real built app without screen control — point JUSPRIN_AGENT_DEV_URL at a copy of the built page with an injected script that logs envelopes to a local http.server and posts messages itself.\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: reference\n  originSessionId: 59133fd8-af56-4958-bb71-9b4812c085b8\n  modified: 2026-10-21T14:27:05.386Z\n---\n\n2026-10-21 (saved-key work, branch claude/api-key-saved-state): Kenneth declined computer-use control of the app, and the Remove path's AppConfig code only runs in the real app. What worked in ~2 minutes:\n\n1. Copy `resources/jusprin/agent/index.html` to a scratch dir, inject a `<script>` right after `<head>` that polls for `window.__jusprinBridge`, wraps its `deliver` to `fetch('http://127.0.0.1:<port>/log?'+JSON)` the envelopes of interest, and sends page messages with `window.wx.postMessage(JSON.stringify({protocol:'jusprin-agent-bridge',version:1,id,type,payload}))`.\n2. Serve the dir with `python3 -m http.server <port> --bind 127.0.0.1 > server.log`; the request log is the test output.\n3. Launch the built binary directly: `JUSPRIN_AGENT_DEV_URL=http://127.0.0.1:<port>/page.html JUSPRIN_AGENT_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:9/v1 <app>/Contents/MacOS/OrcaSlicer --datadir <scratch copy of JusPrin2 with real *_api_key items deleted and TESTONLY keys added>`. The endpoint override keeps model-list and chat traffic off the real providers.\n4. Read the data dir's JusPrin2.conf afterwards for persisted effects; delete the scratch data dir.\n\nThe fork's app bundle id is `io.jusprin.JusPrin` (not com.softfever3d.orca-slicer as [[live-test-built-app-on-mac]] says). Related: [[fake-host-page-fixture]] (page-only states), [[jusprin-worktree-build]].\n\n**Screenshots without screen control (2026-10-21):** add a `snap` command that POSTs `document.documentElement.outerHTML` (mark `document.activeElement` with `data-visual-focus` first) to a tiny local receiver, then strip `<script>`s, replace `:focus-visible` with `[data-visual-focus]`, pin `html,body` to the captured width (headless Chrome has a minimum window width) and screenshot. Keep the page running: the web view's timers stop ~10 s after the window loses visibility, so front the app by pid with `osascript … set frontmost` before every step and run `caffeinate -u -d -t 600`. The app follows the macOS appearance, not `dark_color_mode`; for dark captures deliver an `appearance: dark` envelope to the page and reapply it after any full `state` (a chat turn resends it). A stand-in provider (`JUSPRIN_AGENT_ENDPOINT` → local server that hangs while a flag file exists, else answers 401) produces \"checking\" and \"rejected\" for real.\n---\nname: live-test-built-app-on-mac\ndescription: \"How to launch, see, and drive the locally built JusPrin app on the Mac: the shared bundle id binds tools to the wrong instance, and \\\"on another Space\\\" usually means the window is on the second monitor, not that the user is in full screen.\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: fa2d66ed-e217-440b-aae0-da4164953edc\n  modified: 2026-11-01T19:29:08.107Z\n---\n\nEvery build of the fork (and /Applications/OrcaSlicer.app) shares bundle id `com.softfever3d.orca-slicer`. The desktop-control tools resolve an app by bundle id and bind to whichever instance comes first, so `app_list_windows` returns `[]` and filtered screenshots hide the window you actually launched.\n\n**Working recipe (2026-09-05):** `ditto` the built .app into the scratchpad, `plutil -replace CFBundleIdentifier -string com.jusprin.worktree-test`, `codesign --force --deep -s -`, then `open -n <copy>.app --args <model>` and `request_access` for the new id. `app_screenshot`/`app_click` then work and include popup menus. A display-scope `left_click` on the header did NOT open the fork's PopupWindow menus, but a background `app_click` did; take the pixel-level `zoom` with the display tools afterwards (call `app_release` first). Display-scope `Escape` does not close those popups; a click elsewhere does.\n\nThe MCP discovery file `~/Library/Application Support/JusPrin2/jusprin/mcp.json` points at the newest instance's `http://127.0.0.1:<port>/mcp`; `tests/mcp/probe.py`'s `call()` can drive real tools (e.g. `workspace_inspect`, then `report_slice_review` with sessionId/plateId/sliceResultId) to put the header into the Check-print state without lldb. lldb `expr` cannot call inline accessors like `status_row()`.\n\n**Why:** On 2026-09-01 a verification pass screenshotted the stock app instead of the build; on 2026-09-05 the tools bound to another session's main-repo build.\n\n**How to apply:** Confirm the pid with `pgrep -fl OrcaSlicer.app/Contents/MacOS`; never kill an instance you did not launch. `osascript` System Events by unix id still works to set `frontmost`. See [[jusprin-shell-phase-1-design]] and [[orca-inherited-teardown-crash]].\n\n**\"On another Space\" usually means \"on the other monitor.\"** Cost about ten turns on\n2026-09-09 and produced a wrong report to Kenneth. `app_list_windows` returns\n`is_off_space: true` and clicks are refused with \"this window is on another Space\";\n`app_bring_to_current_space` then fails with \"the user's current Space is a full-screen\napp.\" Both messages are about Spaces, so the natural read is that the user is sitting in\na full-screen app — but with *Displays have separate Spaces* on, a window merely sitting\non the second monitor produces exactly the same symptoms. Kenneth was not in full screen;\nthe harness had opened on the Acer.\n\nTell them apart before saying anything to the user: take a **display-scope** screenshot\n(`app_release`, then `computer_batch` screenshot). Its header names the monitor it\ncaptured and lists the others — if the window shows up there, it is a monitor problem,\nnot a Space problem, and the display-scope tools can drive it immediately. Never conclude\n\"the user is in a full-screen app\" from the background tools' error text alone.\n\nThe same flag also flaps: a window can read `is_off_space: false` and click fine, then\nread `true` a minute later. Clicks delivered while it is true report `ok ... unverified`\nand silently do nothing. **A click that reports \"unverified\" and changes nothing is not\nevidence of an application bug** — on 2026-09-09 that nearly became a filed defect about\nbeing unable to retry after a failed MCP connect. Re-verify on a reachable window before\nconcluding anything about the app.\n\n**Prefer the shell harness over a re-signed app copy for Agent-panel work.**\n`tests/shell/.../JusPrinShellHarness.app` already carries its own bundle id\n(`io.jusprin.shell-harness`), so none of the bundle-id collision above applies, and\n`--manual-unconfigured` lands directly on the dock's not-set-up state — one click from\nthe Agent setup chooser. Build target is `shell_integration_harness`, not `shell_harness`.\n\n**Isolate `$HOME` when testing MCP client setup.** `Mcp::default_catalog_paths()` reads\n`$HOME`, so the flow will happily rewrite the real `~/.cursor/mcp.json`. Launch with","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"e9cda380-b540-49f6-a1de-d183b6bc59f3","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:24:57.376Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"---\nname: live-host-check-via-instrumented-dev-page\ndescription: Test host behaviour in the real built app without screen control — point JUSPRIN_AGENT_DEV_URL at a copy of the built page with an injected script that logs envelopes to a local http.server and posts messages itself.\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: reference\n  originSessionId: 59133fd8-af56-4958-bb71-9b4812c085b8\n  modified: 2026-10-21T14:27:05.386Z\n---\n\n2026-10-21 (saved-key work, branch claude/api-key-saved-state): Kenneth declined computer-use control of the app, and the Remove path's AppConfig code only runs in the real app. What worked in ~2 minutes:\n\n1. Copy `resources/jusprin/agent/index.html` to a scratch dir, inject a `<script>` right after `<head>` that polls for `window.__jusprinBridge`, wraps its `deliver` to `fetch('http://127.0.0.1:<port>/log?'+JSON)` the envelopes of interest, and sends page messages with `window.wx.postMessage(JSON.stringify({protocol:'jusprin-agent-bridge',version:1,id,type,payload}))`.\n2. Serve the dir with `python3 -m http.server <port> --bind 127.0.0.1 > server.log`; the request log is the test output.\n3. Launch the built binary directly: `JUSPRIN_AGENT_DEV_URL=http://127.0.0.1:<port>/page.html JUSPRIN_AGENT_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:9/v1 <app>/Contents/MacOS/OrcaSlicer --datadir <scratch copy of JusPrin2 with real *_api_key items deleted and TESTONLY keys added>`. The endpoint override keeps model-list and chat traffic off the real providers.\n4. Read the data dir's JusPrin2.conf afterwards for persisted effects; delete the scratch data dir.\n\nThe fork's app bundle id is `io.jusprin.JusPrin` (not com.softfever3d.orca-slicer as [[live-test-built-app-on-mac]] says). Related: [[fake-host-page-fixture]] (page-only states), [[jusprin-worktree-build]].\n\n**Screenshots without screen control (2026-10-21):** add a `snap` command that POSTs `document.documentElement.outerHTML` (mark `document.activeElement` with `data-visual-focus` first) to a tiny local receiver, then strip `<script>`s, replace `:focus-visible` with `[data-visual-focus]`, pin `html,body` to the captured width (headless Chrome has a minimum window width) and screenshot. Keep the page running: the web view's timers stop ~10 s after the window loses visibility, so front the app by pid with `osascript … set frontmost` before every step and run `caffeinate -u -d -t 600`. The app follows the macOS appearance, not `dark_color_mode`; for dark captures deliver an `appearance: dark` envelope to the page and reapply it after any full `state` (a chat turn resends it). A stand-in provider (`JUSPRIN_AGENT_ENDPOINT` → local server that hangs while a flag file exists, else answers 401) produces \"checking\" and \"rejected\" for real.\n---\nname: live-test-built-app-on-mac\ndescription: \"How to launch, see, and drive the locally built JusPrin app on the Mac: the shared bundle id binds tools to the wrong instance, and \\\"on another Space\\\" usually means the window is on the second monitor, not that the user is in full screen.\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: fa2d66ed-e217-440b-aae0-da4164953edc\n  modified: 2026-11-01T19:29:08.107Z\n---\n\nEvery build of the fork (and /Applications/OrcaSlicer.app) shares bundle id `com.softfever3d.orca-slicer`. The desktop-control tools resolve an app by bundle id and bind to whichever instance comes first, so `app_list_windows` returns `[]` and filtered screenshots hide the window you actually launched.\n\n**Working recipe (2026-09-05):** `ditto` the built .app into the scratchpad, `plutil -replace CFBundleIdentifier -string com.jusprin.worktree-test`, `codesign --force --deep -s -`, then `open -n <copy>.app --args <model>` and `request_access` for the new id. `app_screenshot`/`app_click` then work and include popup menus. A display-scope `left_click` on the header did NOT open the fork's PopupWindow menus, but a background `app_click` did; take the pixel-level `zoom` with the display tools afterwards (call `app_release` first). Display-scope `Escape` does not close those popups; a click elsewhere does.\n\nThe MCP discovery file `~/Library/Application Support/JusPrin2/jusprin/mcp.json` points at the newest instance's `http://127.0.0.1:<port>/mcp`; `tests/mcp/probe.py`'s `call()` can drive real tools (e.g. `workspace_inspect`, then `report_slice_review` with sessionId/plateId/sliceResultId) to put the header into the Check-print state without lldb. lldb `expr` cannot call inline accessors like `status_row()`.\n\n**Why:** On 2026-09-01 a verification pass screenshotted the stock app instead of the build; on 2026-09-05 the tools bound to another session's main-repo build.\n\n**How to apply:** Confirm the pid with `pgrep -fl OrcaSlicer.app/Contents/MacOS`; never kill an instance you did not launch. `osascript` System Events by unix id still works to set `frontmost`. See [[jusprin-shell-phase-1-design]] and [[orca-inherited-teardown-crash]].\n\n**\"On another Space\" usually means \"on the other monitor.\"** Cost about ten turns on\n2026-09-09 and produced a wrong report to Kenneth. `app_list_windows` returns\n`is_off_space: true` and clicks are refused with \"this window is on another Space\";\n`app_bring_to_current_space` then fails with \"the user's current Space is a full-screen\napp.\" Both messages are about Spaces, so the natural read is that the user is sitting in\na full-screen app — but with *Displays have separate Spaces* on, a window merely sitting\non the second monitor produces exactly the same symptoms. Kenneth was not in full screen;\nthe harness had opened on the Acer.\n\nTell them apart before saying anything to the user: take a **display-scope** screenshot\n(`app_release`, then `computer_batch` screenshot). Its header names the monitor it\ncaptured and lists the others — if the window shows up there, it is a monitor problem,\nnot a Space problem, and the display-scope tools can drive it immediately. Never conclude\n\"the user is in a full-screen app\" from the background tools' error text alone.\n\nThe same flag also flaps: a window can read `is_off_space: false` and click fine, then\nread `true` a minute later. Clicks delivered while it is true report `ok ... unverified`\nand silently do nothing. **A click that reports \"unverified\" and changes nothing is not\nevidence of an application bug** — on 2026-09-09 that nearly became a filed defect about\nbeing unable to retry after a failed MCP connect. Re-verify on a reachable window before\nconcluding anything about the app.\n\n**Prefer the shell harness over a re-signed app copy for Agent-panel work.**\n`tests/shell/.../JusPrinShellHarness.app` already carries its own bundle id\n(`io.jusprin.shell-harness`), so none of the bundle-id collision above applies, and\n`--manual-unconfigured` lands directly on the dock's not-set-up state — one click from\nthe Agent setup chooser. Build target is `shell_integration_harness`, not `shell_harness`.\n\n**Isolate `$HOME` when testing MCP client setup.** `Mcp::default_catalog_paths()` reads\n`$HOME`, so the flow will happily rewrite the real `~/.cursor/mcp.json`. Launch with","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d4534a26-aedc-4972-9564-f0c1cae51c2a","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35/build/arm64","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/first-run-printer-step","slug":"dapper-knitting-moler"}
